window.docContents[74].resolve({"/3___-General-results-of-representation-theory/3___9___-Problems/Formal-deformations-of-representations/#Chapter3___Problem3___9___4":{"contents":"Problem 3.9.4. Let A be an algebra, and let V be a representation of A. Let \\rho : A \\to \\operatorname{End} V. A formal deformation of V is a formal series\n\n\\tilde{\\rho} = \\rho_0 + t\\rho_1 + \\cdots + t^n \\rho_n + \\ldots,\n\nwhere \\rho_i : A \\to \\operatorname{End}(V) are linear maps, \\rho_0 = \\rho, and \\tilde{\\rho}(ab) = \\tilde{\\rho}(a)\\tilde{\\rho}(b).\n\nIf b(t) = 1 + b_1 t + b_2 t^2 + \\ldots, where b_i \\in \\operatorname{End}(V), and \\tilde{\\rho} is a formal deformation of \\rho, then b\\tilde{\\rho}b^{-1} is also a deformation of \\rho, which is said to be isomorphic to \\tilde{\\rho}.\n\n(a) Show that if \\operatorname{Ext}^1(V, V) = 0, then any deformation of \\rho is trivial, i.e., isomorphic to \\rho.\n\n(b) Is the converse to (a) true? (Consider the algebra of dual numbers A = k[x]/x^2.)\n\n\n\n","context":"Introduction to Representation Theory\t3. General results of representation theory\t3.9. Problems\tFormal deformations of representations","header":"Formal deformations of representations","id":"/3___-General-results-of-representation-theory/3___9___-Problems/Formal-deformations-of-representations/#Chapter3___Problem3___9___4"},"/2___-Basic-notions-of-representation-theory/2___11___-Tensor-products/Tensor-product-of-linear-maps/#Chapter2___Discussion_tensor_product_maps":{"contents":"One can also define the tensor product of linear maps. Namely, if A : V \\to V' and B : W \\to W' are linear maps, then one can define the linear map A \\otimes B : V \\otimes W \\to V' \\otimes W' given by the formula (A \\otimes B)(v \\otimes w) = Av \\otimes Bw (check that this is well defined!). The\nmost important properties of tensor products are summarized in the following problem.\n\n\n\n","context":"Introduction to Representation Theory\t2. Basic notions of representation theory\t2.11. Tensor products\tTensor product of linear maps","header":"Tensor product of linear maps","id":"/2___-Basic-notions-of-representation-theory/2___11___-Tensor-products/Tensor-product-of-linear-maps/#Chapter2___Discussion_tensor_product_maps"}});
